# EADOS factory tooling — the .eados-core/ bundle is copied in to (re)generate this repo; it is
# not part of the project's own source.
#
# EXCEPT the run records: every phase procedure appends one (record_run.py), and they are the
# project's own delivery audit trail, not factory tooling. Ignoring them meant they were written,
# reported as written, and never committed — so the trail did not survive a clone and the tools
# that read it (autotune, lesson_audit, the run-record schema gate) saw an empty corpus on every
# fresh checkout, indistinguishable from a genuinely new project (#353).
#
# The shape below is NOT stylistic and must not be "simplified" to `/.eados-core/` plus negations:
# git cannot re-include a path whose PARENT directory is excluded — it never descends into it, so
# the `!` lines would be silently dead. Excluding the CONTENTS (`/*`) at each level and
# re-including the next one down is what makes it work. Verified both ways; the naive form leaves
# the record ignored.
/.eados-core/*
!/.eados-core/learning/
/.eados-core/learning/*
!/.eados-core/learning/runs/

# EADOS command adapters — generated, per HOST, and not this project's source (#372, ADR-0019
# addendum 2026-07-27). `adapter_render.py --host <id>` writes them; they are pointers at the
# procedures inside `.eados-core/`, which the rule above already excludes.
#
# Committing them looked helpful and is not, for two reasons that only became visible once trees
# became per-host:
#   1. A cloned adapter points at `.eados-core/orchestrator/commands/<cmd>.md`, which is NOT in the
#      repository. Whoever clones gets slash commands that resolve to a missing file — worse than
#      absent, because an absent command is obviously absent while a dangling one fails at the
#      point of use and reads as a broken repo.
#   2. It would impose the original author's host on everyone. A committed `.claude/` tree does
#      nothing for a teammate on Gemini, Codex or OpenCode; each generates their own in one command.
#
# The commands are still discoverable without them: `AGENTS.md` §13 carries the full table, and
# `.eados-core/tools/eados.py commands` works on every host, including hosts with no command
# mechanism at all. Delete these lines if you would rather commit your team's tree.
/.claude/commands/eados/
/.gemini/commands/eados/
/.opencode/commands/eados-*
/.eados/adapters/
